"013:001 13:2 And the Lord spoke to Moses, saying,",
"013:002 13:3 Send for you men, and let them spy the land of the Chananites, which I give to the sons of Israel for a possession; one man for a tribe, you shall send them away according to their families, every one of them a prince.",
"013:003 13:4 And Moses sent them out of the wilderness of Pharan by the word of the Lord; all these were the princes of the sons of Israel.",
"013:004 13:5 And these are their names: of the tribe of Ruben, Samuel the son of Zachur.",
"013:005 13:6 Of the tribe of Symeon, Saphat the son of Suri.",
"013:006 13:7 Of the tribe of Judah, Chaleb the son of Jephonne.",
"013:007 13:8 Of the tribe of Issachar, Ilaal the son of Joseph.",
"013:008 13:9 Of the tribe of Ephraim, Ause the son of Naue.",
"013:009 13:10 Of the tribe of Benjamin, Phalti the son of Raphu.",
"013:010 13:11 Of the tribe of Zabulon, Gudiel the son of Sudi.",
"013:011 13:12 Of the tribe of Joseph of the sons of Manasse, Gaddi the son of Susi.",
"013:012 13:13 Of the tribe of Dan, Amiel the son of Gamali.",
"013:013 13:14 Of the tribe of Aser, Sathur the son of Michael.",
"013:014 13:15 Of the tribe of Nephthali, Nabi the son of Sabi.",
"013:015 13:16 Of the tribe of Gad, Gudiel the son of Macchi.",
"013:016 13:17 These are the names of the men whom Moses sent to spy out the land; and Moses called Ause the son of Naue, Joshua.",
"013:017 13:18 And Moses sent them to spy out the land of Chanaan, and said to them, Go up by this wilderness; and you shall go up to the mountain,",
"013:018 13:19 and you shall see the land, what it is, and the people that dwells on it, whether it is strong or weak, or whether they are few or many.",
"013:019 13:20 And what the land is on which they dwell, whether it is good or bad; and what the cities are wherein these dwell, whether they dwell in walled cities or unwalled.",
"013:020 13:21 And what the land is, whether rich or poor; whether there are trees in it or no: and you shall persevere and take of the fruits of the land: and the days were the days of spring, the forerunners of the grape.",
"013:021 13:22 And they went up and surveyed the land from the wilderness of Sin to Rhoob, as men go in to Aemath.",
"013:022 13:23 And they went up by the wilderness, and departed as far as Chebron; and there was Achiman, and Sessi, and Thelami, the progeny of Enach. Now Chebron was built seven years before Tanin of Egypt.",
"013:023 13:24 And they came to the valley of the cluster and surveyed it; and they cut down thence a bough and one cluster of grapes upon it, and bore it on staves, and they took of the pomegranates and the figs.",
"013:024 13:25 And they called that place, The valley of the cluster, because of the cluster which the children of Israel cut down from thence.",
"013:025 13:26 And they returned from thence, having surveyed the land, after forty days.",
"013:026 13:27 And they proceeded and came to Moses and Aaron and all the congregation of the children of Israel, to the wilderness of Pharan Cades; and they brought word to them and to all the congregation, and they showed the fruit of the land:",
"013:027 13:28 and they reported to him, and said, We came into the land into which you sent us, a land flowing with milk and honey; and this is the fruit of it.",
"013:028 13:29 Only the nation that dwells upon it is bold, and they have very great and strong walled towns, and we saw there the children of Enach.",
"013:029 13:30 And Amalec dwells in the land towards the south: and the Chettite and the Evite, and the Jebusite, and the Amorite dwells in the hill country: and the Chananite dwells by the sea, and by the river Jordan.",
"013:030 13:31 And Chaleb stayed the people from speaking before Moses, and said to him, Nay, but we will go up by all means, and will inherit it, for we shall surely prevail against them.",
"013:031 13:32 But the men that went up together with him said, We will not go up, for we shall not by any means be able to go up against the nation, for it is much stronger than we.",
"013:032 13:33 And they brought a horror of that land which they surveyed upon the children of Israel, saying, The land which we passed by to survey it, is a land that eats up its inhabitants; and all the people whom we saw in it are men of extraordinary stature.",
"013:033 13:34 And there we saw the giants; and we were before them as locusts, yes even so were we before them."
