"024:001 And when Balaam saw that it pleased God to bless Israel, he did not go according to his custom to meet the omens, but turned his face towards the wilderness.",
"024:002 And Balaam lifted up his eyes, and sees Israel encamped by their tribes; and the Spirit of God came upon him.",
"024:003 And he took up his parable and said, Balaam son of Beor says, the man who sees truly says,",
"024:004 he says who hears the oracle of the Mighty One, who saw a vision of God in sleep; his eyes were opened:",
"024:005 How goodly are your habitations, Jacob, and your tents, Israel!",
"024:006 as shady groves, and as gardens by a river, and as tents which God pitched, and as cedars by the waters.",
"024:007 There shall come a man out of his seed, and he shall rule over many nations; and the kingdom of Gog shall be exalted, and his kingdom shall be increased.",
"024:008 God led him out of Egypt; he has as it were the glory of a unicorn: he shall consume the nations of his enemies, and he shall drain their marrow, and with his darts he shall shoot through the enemy.",
"024:009 He lay down, he rested as a lion, and as a young lion; who shall stir him up? they that bless you are blessed, and they that curse you are cursed.",
"024:010 And Balac was angry with Balaam, and clapped his hands together; and Balac said to Balaam, I called you to curse my enemy, and behold you have decidedly blessed him this third time.",
"024:011 Now therefore flee to your place: I said, I will honour you, but now the Lord has deprived you of glory.",
"024:012 And Balaam said to Balac, Did I not speak to your messengers also whom you sent to me, saying,",
"024:013 If Balac should give me his house full of silver and gold, I shall not be able to transgress the word of the Lord to make it good or bad by myself; whatever things God shall say, them will I speak.",
"024:014 And now, behold, I return to my place; come, I will advise you of what this people shall do to your people in the last days.",
"024:015 And he took up his parable and said, Balaam the son of Beor says, the man who sees truly says,",
"024:016 hearing the oracles of God, receiving knowledge from the Most High, and having seen a vision of God in sleep; his eyes were opened.",
"024:017 I will point to him, but not now; I bless him, but he draws not near: a star shall rise out of Jacob, a man shall spring out of Israel; and shall crush the princes of Moab, and shall spoil all the sons of Seth.",
"024:018 And Edom shall be an inheritance, and Esau his enemy shall be an inheritance of Israel, and Israel wrought valiantly.",
"024:019 And one shall arise out of Jacob, and destroy out of the city him that escapes.",
"024:020 And having seen Amalec, he took up his parable and said, Amalec is the first of the nations; yet his seed shall perish.",
"024:021 And having seen the Kenite, he took up his parable and said, your dwelling-place is strong; yet though you should put your nest in a rock,",
"024:022 and though Beor should have a skilfully contrived hiding-place, the Assyrians shall carry you away captive.",
"024:023 And he looked upon Og, and took up his parable and said, Oh, oh, who shall live, when God shall do these things?",
"024:024 And one shall come forth from the hands of the Citians, and shall afflict Assur, and shall afflict the Hebrews, and they shall perish together.",
"024:025 And Balaam rose up and departed and returned to his place, and Balac went to his own home."
