"030:001 30:2 And Moses spoke to the heads of the tribes of the children of Israel, saying, This is the thing which the Lord has commanded.",
"030:002 30:3 Whatsoever man shall vow a vow to the Lord, or swear an oath, or bind himself with an obligation upon his soul, he shall not break his word; all that shall come out of his mouth he shall do.",
"030:003 30:4 And if a woman shall vow a vow to the Lord, or bind herself with an obligation in her youth in her father's house; and her father should hear her vows and her obligations, wherewith she has bound her soul, and her father should hold his peace at her, then all her vows shall stand,",
"030:004 30:5 and all the obligations with which she has bound her soul, shall remain to her.",
"030:005 30:6 But if her father straitly forbid her in the day in which he shall hear all her vows and her obligations, which she has contracted upon her soul, they shall not stand; and the Lord shall hold her guiltless, because her father forbade her.",
"030:006 30:7 But if she should be indeed married, and her vows be upon her according to the utterance of her lips, the obligations which she has contracted upon her soul;",
"030:007 30:8 and her husband should hear, and hold his peace at her in the day in which he should hear, then thus shall all her vows be binding, and her obligations, which she has contracted upon her soul shall stand.",
"030:008 30:9 But if her husband should straitly forbid her in the day in which he should hear her, none of her vows or obligations which she has contracted upon her soul shall stand, because her husband has disallowed her, and the Lord shall hold her guiltless.",
"030:009 30:10 And the vow of a widow and of her that is put away, whatever she shall bind upon her soul, shall stand to her.",
"030:010 30:11 And if her vow be made in the house of her husband, or the obligation upon her soul with an oath,",
"030:011 30:12 and her husband should hear, and hold his peace at her, and not disallow her, then all her vows shall stand, and all the obligations which she contracted against her soul, shall stand against her.",
"030:012 30:13 But if her husband should utterly cancel the vow in the day in which he shall hear it, none of the things which shall proceed out of her lips in her vows, and in the obligations contracted upon her soul, shall stand to her; her husband has cancelled them, and the Lord shall hold her guiltless.",
"030:013 30:14 Every vow, and every binding oath to afflict her soul, her husband shall confirm it to her, or her husband shall cancel it.",
"030:014 30:15 But if he be wholly silent at her from day to day, then shall he bind upon her all her vows; and he shall confirm to her the obligations which she has bound upon herself, because he held his peace at her in the day in which he heard her.",
"030:015 30:16 And if her husband should in any wise cancel them after the day in which he heard them, then he shall bear his iniquity.",
"030:016 30:17 These are the ordinances which the Lord commanded Moses, between a man and his wife, and between a father and daughter in her youth in the house of her father."
