"032:009 And they went up to the valley of the cluster, and spied the land, and turned aside the heart of the children of Israel, that they should not go into the land, which the Lord gave them.",
"032:010 And the Lord was very angry in that day, and swore, saying,",
"032:011 Surely these men who came up out of Egypt from twenty years old and upward, who know good and evil, shall not see the land which I swore to give to Abraam and Isaac and Jacob, for they have not closely followed after me:",
"032:012 save Caleb the son of Jephonne, who was set apart, and Joshua the son of Naue, for they closely followed after the Lord.",
"032:013 And the Lord was very angry with Israel; and for forty years he caused them to wander in the wilderness, until all the generation which did evil in the sight of the Lord was extinct.",
"032:014 Behold, you are risen up in the room of your fathers, a combination of sinful men, to increase yet farther the fierce wrath of the Lord against Israel.",
"032:015 For you will turn away from him to desert him yet once more in the wilderness, and you will sin against this whole congregation.",
"032:016 And they came to him, and said, We will build here folds for our cattle, and cities for our possessions;",
"032:017 and we will arm ourselves and go as an advanced guard before the children of Israel, until we shall have brought them into their place; and our possessions shall remain in walled cities because of the inhabitants of the land.",
"032:018 We will not return to our houses till the children of Israel shall have been distributed, each to his own inheritance.",
"032:019 And we will not any longer inherit with them from the other side of Jordan and onwards, because we have our full inheritance on the side beyond Jordan eastward.",
"032:020 And Moses said to them, If you will do according to these words, if you will arm yourselves before the Lord for battle,",
"032:021 and every one of you will pass over Jordan fully armed before the Lord, until his enemy be destroyed from before his face,",
"032:022 and the land shall be subdued before the Lord, then afterwards you shall return, and be guiltless before the Lord, and as regards Israel; and this land shall be to you for a possession before the Lord.",
"032:023 But if you will not do so, you will sin against the Lord; and you shall know your sin, when afflictions shall come upon you.",
"032:024 And you shall build for yourselves cities for your store, and folds for your cattle; and you shall do that which proceeds out of your mouth.",
"032:025 And the sons of Ruben and the sons of Gad spoke to Moses, saying, Your servants will do as our lord commands.",
"032:026 Our store, and our wives, and all our cattle shall be in the cities of Galaad.",
